<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Italian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1946 CE – present · capital Rome</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Modern Italy, a democratic republic since the referendum of 1946 and a founding member of the European Communities and NATO.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 2 June 1946 Italians voted in a referendum to abolish the monarchy of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enrico-de-nicola">Enrico De Nicola</a> became provisional head of state. A Constituent Assembly drafted a new constitution, which came into force on 1 January 1948.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> is a parliamentary republic with a president as head of state. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-democracy-italy">Christian Democrat</a> governments led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcide-de-gasperi">Alcide De Gasperi</a> and his successors anchored it in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> in 1949 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">European Economic Community</a>, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rome">Treaty of Rome</a> in 1957. The economic miracle of the 1950s and 1960s transformed the country, though it suffered political terrorism in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/years-of-lead-italy">Years of Lead</a> and a lasting gap between north and south.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The Tangentopoli corruption scandals of 1992 swept away the old party system. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> adopted the euro in 1999 and remains a major European economy; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sergio-mattarella">Sergio Mattarella</a> has been president since 2015.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/italian-republic.jpg" alt="Italian Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See below. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts